## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 0133509772c96703549939c1db7fbc7c64123578

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I ran `git log --follow -- ConventionJdt.java` to get the full history of the file touched by the fix, then `git log -p --follow` to inspect every historical diff, grepping for `compilerComplianceLevel` occurrences across all commits.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `0133509` ("Thu Dec 1 16:20:21 2016 -0800", by the same author, ~1h51m before the fix) refactored `ConventionJdt.compilerComplianceLevel(String)` from a field+Action-class design into an inline lambda. Before the refactor:
```java
public void compilerComplianceLevel(String compilerComplianceLevel) {
    this.compilerComplianceLevel = JavaVersion.toVersion(compilerComplianceLevel); // field, type JavaVersion
}
...
JDT_COMPLIANCE_PROPS.forEach(p -> props.put(p, complianceLevel.toString())); // complianceLevel is a JavaVersion
```
After the refactor in `0133509`:
```java
public void compilerComplianceLevel(String compilerComplianceLevel) {
    ...
    extension.workspaceProp(JDT_CORE_PREFS, props -> {
        JDT_COMPLIANCE_PROPS.forEach(p -> props.put(p, compilerComplianceLevel.toString()));
        ...
    });
}
```
Here `compilerComplianceLevel` is the raw `String` method parameter (the field and `JavaVersion.toVersion(...)` conversion were deleted), so `.toString()` on it is a no-op that just returns the unnormalized input string instead of the properly normalized Java version string (e.g. `JavaVersion.toVersion("1.6").toString()` → normalized `"1.6"`, but also handles inputs like `"6"`, `"JavaVersion.VERSION_1_6"`, etc., which the raw-string path would leave un-normalized).

**(3) Evidence:** The fix commit `a9a3e6c` reverses exactly this: it changes `compilerComplianceLevel.toString()` back to `JavaVersion.toVersion(compilerComplianceLevel).toString()`, restoring the normalization that was lost when the field/`JavaVersion` conversion was dropped in `0133509`. There are no other commits touching this file between `0133509` and `a9a3e6c` that could have introduced the regression, so `0133509` is the sole bug-introducing commit.

I'm confident in this identification — the fix is a direct, minimal reversal of the exact line changed in `0133509`, with no intervening modifications to that code path.

